Where needed.

The rationale is as follows:

1. It's behind DEBUG_ENABLED because in some cases (not all of them) it may be expensive enough to do this check in the exported game. But it should be done while in Editor builds (when it is paramount to detect it)
2. It must not fail / early out. The most likely scenario is that the user is running the Editor on a Desktop GPU (unless you're on an ARM mac). The GPU command will render fine. But the editor will show you the error. This is IMO the best user-friendly outcome: rendering happens the way user intended; but the user is notified something is wrong.
3. User will notice this error early in his big monster machine. Not late when he decides to deploy to a phone (and not all phones, e.g. RDNA phones are not tilers so the user won't notice anything wrong).

I've tested this and Mobile does not trigger the error, but Forward+ of course does; because it is as you say: SSAO and others need to sample from the Depth Buffer.

